+// The 3D scene at its own internal scale, the 2D drawn over it at the configured
+// one (UpscaleMultiplier): Magatama's resolution scale changes the 3D only, the
+// HUD and menus stay at the display's resolution. A draw that tests or writes
+// depth, and any draw after one until the next 2D sprite without depth, uses the
+// scene scale; other draws the configured scale. The render target is resampled
+// when a field moves between the two (the texture cache's per-target scale, as
+// for PCSX2's native scaling). 0 = off (stock). Applies from the next draw.
+void GSRrvSetSceneScale(float scale);
 // A sprite the bridge has moved (its X is no longer the game's) cannot have the
 // texels it spans found from its position, so the bridge finds them from the
 // game's coordinates, writes them to U and marks the sprite: RoundSpriteOffset()
